kind: fix

upstream: not for V-HACD, whose debug writers are its own to keep.

The header carries OBJ writers for debugging (VertexIndex::SaveAsObj,
VoxelHull's SaveVoxelMesh, SaveOBJ and WriteOBJ) that nothing calls. The
linker drops them, so no wheel imports fopen, but the source still names
it, and the extension is held to writing no files at all: compile them out,
so what `uv run scripts threads` scans opens nothing, and that scan needs
no exception for vendored code.
Covered by: `uv run scripts threads` (it fails on any fopen the build
compiles), tests/test_vhacd.py, fuzz/vhacd.cpp.

